# Appearance typography

Font family and size come from **Settings → Appearance** (`useDashboardAppearanceStore`).

## CSS variables (set on `html` + `.dash-appearance-scope`)

| Token | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `--dash-font-family` | All dashboard UI |
| `--dash-body-size` | Inputs, selects, detail values |
| `--dash-label-size` | Form/detail field labels |
| `--dash-text-xs` … `--dash-text-2xl` | Tailwind `text-xs` … `text-2xl` |

## Presets (base / xs)

- **Small:** 14px / 12px
- **Medium:** 16px / 14px (default)
- **Large:** 18px / 16px

## Do

- Use `text-[length:var(--dash-body-size)]` or `text-[length:var(--dash-label-size)]` on custom controls
- Use Tailwind `text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base` (they scale with appearance)
- Use `FieldLabel`, `fieldLabelClassName`, `surfaceInputClassName` from `@/shared/ui/field-primitives`

## Avoid

- Hardcoded `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`, `text-[12px]` in dashboard UI (legacy sizes are remapped in `globals.css`, but prefer scalable tokens)
- Fixed `text-sm` on detail values when appearance body size is preferred

Update scale in `src/features/dashboard/utils/appearance-typography.util.ts`.
